Results and discussion
Scanning electron microscopy revealed the spherical morphology of the C103 powder and its dendritic structure which was formed
during the cooling stage of ultrasonic atomization. The powder was characterized by narrow particle size distribution and high
sphericity factor (Figure 4). Such material will be characterized by advantageous bulk density and flowability beneficially
influencing the powder bed fusion processes20).
Figure 4 SEM image of niobium C103 alloy powder: (A) macroscopic view, and (B) its structure
During the inspection of the cross-section, HfO2 precipitates were not detected using EDS. Oxygen can highly impact the material
performance which is mainly used in critical applications21). EDS analysis of the cross-section of the powder confirmed no
segregation of the elements in the observed scale.
